  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "URaamPIemvlyejG0QasltupttV8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:29.826Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Orchestration Cluster API gained a user-task audit-log search marked *\"Added in 8.9\"*, and Camunda's own roadmap frames the pre-8.9 state as exactly the gap in question: organisations lacked a unified trail recording who did what, when, and to which entities. Release 8.9.16 shipped on 2026-08-14; the audit-log follow-up epic closed on 2026-03-10.\n\nRetention ships disabled (`retention.enabled: false`, 30-day minimum age when switched on), which is a genuinely better default than most tools in this class.\n\nThe residual technical differences are real but too subtle to carry an argument: the log is documented as \"Eventually Consistent\" rather than transactionally coupled to the decision, and records live in ordinary mutable Elasticsearch indices with no hash chain. A demo asserting that Camunda cannot say who decided something would be factually wrong against 8.9 and corrected in the room.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T08:45:29.826765Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:29.826769Z"
    }
  },
